SRC/soelim -- soelim, as built for OS-9/68000=============================================ORIG holds the post as comp.sources.unix carried it.  soelim.c differs inone token: its usage message passed *argv[0], the first character of theprogram's name, to a %s, where argv[0] was meant.  Run bare at a terminal itprinted `Usage:   [ file ...' with the name missing (on a system thatchecks addresses it would have faulted); now it prints its own name.  Thefix is right on any system, so it is made outright rather than under OSK.